      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "tropica",
      "sourceUrl": "https://tropica.com/en/plants/plantdetails/Cryptocorynecrispatula(125TC)/18756",
      "html": "<ul><li>Origin: Asia</li><li>Growth rate: medium</li><li>Height: 20 - 30+ cm</li><li>Light demand: low</li><li>CO2 demand: low</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "tropica",
      "sourceUrl": "https://tropica.com/en/plants/plantdetails/Cryptocorynecrispatula(125TC)/18756",
      "html": "<p>Cryptocoryne crispatula var. balansae is from the limestone mountains of Southern Thailand, where the water can be very hard.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "maintenance",
      "source": "tropica",
      "sourceUrl": "https://tropica.com/en/plants/plantdetails/Cryptocorynecrispatula(125TC)/18756",
      "html": "<p>Not very demanding, but appreciates a nutritious substrate and good light. Like many other Cryptocorynes it needs to acclimatize before growth starts in earnest. Leaves become 20-60 cm long and the single rosette plant becomes 15-20 cm wide. Place it in the rear part of the tank, from where the leaves may float beautifully on the water surface.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "tropica",
      "sourceUrl": "https://tropica.com/en/plants/plantdetails/Cryptocorynecrispatula(125TC)/18756",
      "html": "<p>Supplied as aquarium plant from tissue culture in a closed cup. The leaves are either entirely green or maroon.</p>"
    }
  ],
